Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 19:59:14 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 585/588] fix(desktop): a stale-list row still opens and names
 its connection as not responding [daveey]
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

When the owner's last session list failed (a busy local backend whose event loop
stalled), mergeOfflineFallback turned its live rows into offline_cached rows with
no offline_gateway/offline_synced_at, and useOfflineFallback refused to open them
with "its gateway is offline ... (cached, never synced)". The gateway was running.

Rows retained from a failed list with no replica copy are now stamped
offline_stale_list. Opening one shows "<connection> is not responding ...
Trying to open this chat anyway." and calls resumeSession (its own timeout
applies). Replica rows of an unreachable gateway stay refused. The row's
offline mark says "Not responding · <connection>, showing its last list".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
